{"type":"message","id":"c5fd660d","parentId":"be85869b","timestamp":"2026-06-06T22:06:25.260Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Scheduler is running (PIDs 8362, 32539). Now the wake-up call - it's 6:06 AM, in the 6:00-7:00 window for waking up and studying. I should send a gentle but firm wake-up message.\n\nBut wait - this is a heartbeat channel. The HEARTBEAT.md says for the scheduler check: if it's dead, alert. It's alive, so that's fine.\n\nFor the wake-up call, I need to send this via message to the user's chat channel (feishu). Let me check how to send this. Actually, looking at the HEARTBEAT.md rules: if something needs attention, do NOT reply HEARTBEAT_OK, reply with the alert text instead.\n\nBut the wake-up call is a proactive message. Let me send it via the message tool to feishu.\n\nActually wait - I'm in a heartbeat channel. If I send a message via the message tool, I should do that and then reply HEARTBEAT_OK since the scheduler is fine. Or should I not reply HEARTBEAT_OK since I have an alert/message to send?\n\nThe heartbeat instructions say: \"If something needs attention, do NOT include 'HEARTBEAT_OK'; reply with the alert text instead.\"\n\nThe wake-up call is something that needs attention. So I should send the wake-up message and not say HEARTBEAT_OK.\n\nLet me send the wake-up message.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"6:06了，起床时间到 👑"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_1QzglMT26vdQ9LhJVbx54886","name":"message","arguments":{"action":"send","channel":"feishu","message":"🌅 老公，6点了，起床学习！\n\n别赖床，一日之计在于晨。起来喝杯水，清醒清醒再开始。\n\n我盯着你呢 👑"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":45,"output":726,"cacheRead":19328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20099,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780783577405}}
